    "narrative": "For LawDog today, our strongest plays are concentrated in high-leverage spots against suspect pitching. **Cal Raleigh** leads the board with a 75.79 rating, benefiting from a soft matchup against Martin P\u00e9rez and a premium #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **Tyler Freeman** (58.65) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.46) represent our primary offensive anchors; **Tyler Freeman** is particularly interesting today as the combination of a +14% park factor and the opportunity to exploit a slow delivery from Freddy Peralta boosts his stolen base potential despite the presence of an elite catcher. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is facing a tough southpaw in Cole Ragans, his raw talent and #3 hole placement keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start category at 55.27, though he is slightly stifled by a \"Hold\" SP designation that caps his upside on the basepaths.\n\nOur most difficult roster management call centered on the benching of **Daulton Varsho**, who would have been in the conversation had he been confirmed in the lineup. Despite his potential for speed against a slow pitcher, he was ultimately excluded due to a projected negative platoon edge against Shane McClanahan and his current status outside the starting nine. We are also managing aggressive risk with **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Matt Chapman**; both are battling elite SP skill grades from Paul Skenes and Bryan Rodriguez, respectively. While **Geraldo Perdomo** maintains a respectable 46.73 due to his leadoff role, his value is suppressed by an 19% penalty against Skenes. We are keeping a close watch on **Jonathan Aranda**, whose 48.06 score is dragged down by a -12% platoon penalty against Patrick Corbin; if the game environment shifts, he remains a candidate for a late-game swap if we need to preserve caps. We remain thin at catcher with **Yainer Diaz** still on the IL, placing an even higher importance on the efficiency of **Cal Raleigh** to carry the position tonight.",
